<%# The page tree column of a Pages screen, for a full answer only. The
    column stands outside `#content` and outlives a frame navigation, and a
    frame answer keeps only `#content`, so a tree drawn into one would be
    read and sent for nothing; the tree's script moves the selection to the
    page the frame opened (`admin--pages--tree`, "The selected row"). The
    check is the view's and never `TreeComponent`'s: a stream's
    `replace("tree")` draws the component whatever the request's headers, and
    a component that drew nothing there would leave the column blank. %>
<% unless turbo_frame_request? %>
  <% content_for :tree do %>
    <%= render Admin::PagesScreen::TreeComponent.new(root: root_page, selected: selected, locale: admin_locale, url_options: admin_url_options,
          open_cookie: cookies[TreeOpenSet::COOKIE]) %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
